  <paragraph>Be careful when you are asked to factor a binomial as there are several options!</paragraph>
  <example number="6.36">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Factor completely: $$24y^{2} - 150.$$</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$24y^{2} - 150$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Is there a GCF? Yes, 6.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Factor out the GCF.</cell>
            <cell>$$6\left( {4y^{2} - 25} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>In the parentheses, is it a binomial, trinomial or are there more than three terms? Binomial.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Is it a sum? No.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Is it a difference? Of squares or cubes? Yes, squares.</cell>
            <cell>$$6\left( {\left( {2y} \right)^{2} - (5)^{2}} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Write as a product of conjugates.</cell>
            <cell>$$6\left( {2y - 5} \right)\left( {2y + 5} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$\text{Is the expression factored completely?}$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$\text{Neither binomial can be factored.}$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Check:</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$\text{Multiply.}$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$6\left( {2y - 5} \right)\left( {2y + 5} \right)$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$6\left( {4y^{2} - 25} \right)$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$24y^{2} - 150✓$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
  <note type="practice" source_type="Try It" title="Try It" number="6.71">
    <paragraph>Factor completely: $$16x^{3} - 36x.$$</paragraph>
  </note>
